Author: Yukihiro "Matz" Matsumoto <matz@ruby.or.jp>
Date:   Sat Aug 1 13:54:43 2026 +0900

    vm.c: store through the refreshed regs after a VM re-entry

    `regs[a] = mrb_ary_splat(...)` computes the address of regs[a] before
    the call, so when the callee re-enters the VM and stack_extend()
    reallocates the stack, the store lands in the freed buffer. Both sites
    already refreshed `ci` afterwards, which is too late for a store whose
    destination was fixed on the way in.

    Take the value first and assign through the refreshed `regs`, the way
    the sibling branch of OP_ARYCAT already does. OP_GETIV had the same
    shape via mrb_iv_get().

    Found via clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-mruby_fuzzer-4936203238178816,
    where a user-defined `to_a` grows the stack during a splat.

    Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

